From f73b9e61e366ee460bf39224264ef7ba685f51fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gabriel Fernandez <gabriel.fernandez@foss.st.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Feb 2026 11:29:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: soc: st: add STM32 hog driver to enable
 always-on clocks

Add the STM32 hog platform driver, which retrieves all clocks referenced
by its Device Tree node and enables them in bulk at probe time.
These clocks are then kept running for the lifetime of the device, and are
disabled on driver removal.

This helper is intended to ensure that critical SoC resources or
peripherals remain clocked early in the boot process, even when no
functional driver has been probed yet.

Signed-off-by: Gabriel Fernandez <gabriel.fernandez@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: I5ef419d9ec052b9fafab5d79dbd10c273b2123fb
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/linux-stm32/+/536397
